\begin{theorem}[Existence and Attractor of Closure]
Assume $$ F $$ is locally Lipschitz and the memory kernel satisfies $$ \int_0^\infty \|K_t(\tau)\|\,d\tau&lt;\infty $$ uniformly in $$ t $$, with a strict contraction on average. Then the flow admits a unique compact global attractor $$ \mathcal{A} $$; if $$ T $$ is the time-$$ \Delta $$ stroboscopic map of this flow, $$ T $$ is idempotent on $$ \mathcal{A} $$ and equals the transjective closure on its basin.
