\section{Cohesive \texorpdfstring{$$ \infty $$}{âˆž}-Topos Renormalization Principle}
\label{sec:cohesiverg}
\textbf{Abstract.}
Renormalization (Â§ 23) describes how epistemic parameters evolve with scale.
In cohesive âˆž-topoi, scale transformations act as endofunctors preserving the adjoint modalities
$$ \Pi\dashv\flat\dashv\Gamma\dashv\sharp $$.
This section formalizes the renormalization group as a functor on cohesive âˆž-categories,
proves existence of a universal renormalization natural transformation,
and identifies understanding as the fixed object invariant under all such transformations.
The result closes Part II by uniting scale, category, and cognition into one functorial law.
